-- title:
--   Divisibility by a prime over 𝔽ₚ descends along Xᵢ ↦ Xᵢ^{p^n}
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $K$ a field that is an algebra over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, and $\sigma$ an arbitrary index type for the variables; fix $n \in \mathbb{N}$. Let $f \in \mathbb{F}_p[X_i : i \in \sigma]$ be a prime element of the multivariate polynomial ring over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, and let $g \in K[X_i : i \in \sigma]$. Write $\psi$ for the $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebra endomorphism of $K[X_i : i \in \sigma]$ determined by $X_i \mapsto X_i^{p^n}$ for all $i \in \sigma$, that is, `MvPolynomial.aeval` applied to the family $i \mapsto X_i^{p^n}$, and let $f_K$ denote the image of $f$ under the coefficient map induced by $\mathbb{Z}/p \to K$. The assertion is: if $\psi(g)$ lies in the principal ideal generated by $f_K$, then $g$ itself lies in that ideal. Note that $\sigma$ carries no finiteness hypothesis and that $K$ need not be perfect or even separably generated over $\mathbb{F}_p$; only primality of $f$ over the prime field is assumed.
--
--   The statement is the injectivity of the $n$-fold relative ($K$-linear) Frobenius on the hypersurface ring $K[X_i]/(f_K)$ for $f$ prime and defined over the prime field; primality cannot be dropped, as $f = X^p$, $g = X$ shows. It is used to extend the relative Frobenius of the Drinfeld curve to its function field, in [`DrinfeldCurve.exists_algHom_drinfeldFunctionField_apply_x_eq_pow`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.exists_algHom_drinfeldFunctionField_apply_x_eq_pow).
